Copyright 2026 The agdablueprint authors

This product includes software developed for blueprint-style coordination of
Agda formalization projects.

It builds on, and is conceptually derived from, the following projects:

  - plasTeX (https://github.com/plastex/plastex), the LaTeX-to-DOM engine.
  - plastexdepgraph (https://github.com/PatrickMassot/plastexdepgraph),
    the proof-assistant-agnostic dependency-graph plasTeX plugin that
    agdablueprint loads alongside its own plugin. Apache-2.0.
  - leanblueprint (https://github.com/PatrickMassot/leanblueprint), the Lean
    blueprint tool by Patrick Massot. Apache-2.0. agdablueprint's CLI shape and
    web theme follow leanblueprint, and its LaTeX macro layer
    (macros/common.tex, macros/print.tex, agdablueprint.sty) is adapted directly
    from leanblueprint's templates: the \uses / \proves print definitions, the
    package stub (\DeclareOption*{}, \ProcessOptions, \graphcolor), and the
    theorem-environment block are reused largely verbatim.

The change made to those files is the replacement of leanblueprint's Lean-named
status macros (\lean, \leanok, \mathlibok) with Agda-flavored ones (\agda,
\agdaok, \agdanotready, \stdlibok); agdablueprint also adds an Agda declaration
checker in place of leanblueprint's Lean-specific tooling.
